/-!
# Infinite-rank Weil theory over Spec ℤ

The curve proof of Weil's theorem in three steps — a crude count at every level, a self-improvement
by finite-rank elimination, and the functional equation — rebuilt at infinite rank. Weil towers
(`z ↦ z̄`, `z ↦ 1/z`), level sums, the exceptional rank that decides Turán windows, the rank barrier,
elimination for well-founded towers, the exceptional coordinate (ZAL, AAL, isolated tops), models of
the functional equation with any finite layer, the towers of `ζ`, Wolff towers, the count of a tower
and the strength of the crude step, prime collisions, and the precision cost of forced vanishing. See
`InfiniteRankWeilTheory/README.md`.
-/
